{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>So He released.</b> The angel <b>from him; then</b> she understood that he had come to kill him on account of the circumcision." "<b>She said: A bridegroom of blood, for the circumcisions.</b> My bridegroom would have been killed on account of the circumcision." "<b>For the circumcisions.</b> On account of the circumcisions. It is a noun, and the lamed serves in the sense of 'on account of,' as in ״וְאָמַר פַּרְעֹה לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ (Exodus 14), and Onkelos rendered דָּמִים as 'on account of the blood of circumcision.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:37.186611970Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}